Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Tate-McRae.md` and appended a `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom. No body edits made.

**The two biggest flags:**

1. **The Morgan Wallen omission is also a factual error.** Section 6 lists "Her first No. 1 single" as a clean milestone. Her first Hot 100 No. 1 *is* the Wallen feature "What I Want" (May 2025) — "Sports car" peaked at 16, "greedy" at 3, and she has no solo No. 1. So the draft banks the trophy and omits that it came attached to the worst fan revolt of her career ("MAGA," "Tate McRae-cist"). Her own explanation is the most on-thesis sentence in her public record: *"It was just about the song for me. I didn't realize how much a song would be connected to all the other factors, and it really shocked me."* A Three optimizing the deliverable and being genuinely blindsided that the deliverable had a context. Fixing the fact hands the piece its best beat. Still generating coverage as of Aug 3, 2026.

2. **"you broke me first" and "greedy" are never named.** The draft jumps from "one day" (2017) to *So Close to What* (2025), skipping the two songs — 1.9B and 1B+ streams — that actually made her famous. A reader who knows her from the radio finishes the profile without meeting the song they know her from.

Also flagged: the sexualization discourse as the missing half of "purple lace bra" (she has better wound-vocabulary on it than the draft's "seen not heard" reading), the absent Britney "blueprint" comparison, an industry-plant promise in the intro that never pays off, and section 5 running as a six-quote stack.
